(18,160,829,$q$The Bund at night$q$,$q$Lujiazui's towers lit up across the Huangpu, from the riverside promenade.$q$,$q$35mm / 85mm$q$,'night','20:45','must','planned',0,'area',700,31.23736,121.488599,$q$The raised riverside promenade along the Bund, opposite the Pearl Tower. The lights go off around 10pm.$q$,$q$- The whole Lujiazui skyline over the river — 35mm, braced on the promenade wall.
- People at the railing, silhouetted against the lit towers — 85mm, from behind.
- A lit tour boat sliding across the frame — 35mm at about 1/4s, so it streaks a little.
- Turn around: the old bank buildings floodlit gold — 35mm.$q$,$q$No tripod: brace on the promenade wall. 35mm at f/2, 1/4–1/8s, ISO 1600, 2-second timer. People at the rail: 85mm at f/1.8, 1/125s, ISO 3200–6400. If you bring the mini tripod, this is a spot for it: ISO 100, f/8, 5–15s for smooth water.$q$,false),
(18,161,831,$q$West Bund riverside$q$,$q$Old coal-wharf structures, the Long Museum's concrete vaults and the riverside path.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'morning','10:00','want','planned',1,'area',600,31.185916,121.460193,$q$Start at the Long Museum (West Bund); the riverside path runs right outside it, along the old coal-loading bridge.$q$,$q$- The Long Museum's concrete umbrella vaults with one person for scale — 20-70.
- The old coal-hopper bridge against the sky — 20-70 at 20.
- Skaters, cyclists and dog walkers on the river path — 70-200 from a distance.$q$,$q$Photo rules inside the galleries change with each show; check the signs.$q$,false),
(18,161,833,$q$Wukang Mansion$q$,$q$The 1924 wedge-shaped apartment block where the roads meet.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'afternoon','15:00','want','planned',2,'spot',null,31.206256,121.433729,$q$At the junction of Huaihai Middle Road and Wukang Road, facing the building's narrow prow. Everyone shoots from the same crossing; walk back up Huaihai Road for the long lens.$q$,$q$- The prow with plane trees and traffic in front — 70-200 at 100–200 from up Huaihai Road, so the street compresses.
- A cyclist or bus passing the point of the building — 70-200.
- Wukang Road's plane trees turning yellow, villa gates and walls — 20-70.
- The side streets behind the mansion: laundry, bikes, people on chairs — 70-200, discreetly.$q$,null,false),
(18,161,834,$q$Xintiandi at night$q$,$q$The restored stone-gate (shikumen) lanes lit up for the evening.$q$,$q$35mm / 85mm$q$,'night','19:00','maybe','planned',3,'area',300,31.223407,121.4701,$q$The lanes of Xintiandi, a few minutes' walk from the Andaz.$q$,$q$- Grey brick and black-lacquered gateways in warm light, people passing — 35mm.
- Faces at the outdoor tables under the heaters — 85mm wide open.
- Reflections on the paving stones if it has rained.$q$,null,false),
(18,162,835,$q$The Bund at 7am$q$,$q$Tai chi, joggers and dancers on the promenade, with low sun on the old bank fronts.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'morning','07:00','must','planned',4,'area',700,31.23736,121.488599,$q$The same riverside promenade as Friday night. Sun up about 6:30.$q$,$q$- Sun straight onto the Bund's stone fronts (they face east, so this is their light) — 70-200 to pick out the domes and the clock tower.
- Tai chi groups and ballroom dancers on the promenade — 70-200 from a polite distance.
- Lujiazui's towers in morning haze across the river — 20-70.
- A jogger crossing the frame against the river — 70-200.$q$,null,false),
(18,162,838,$q$Waibaidu Bridge at blue hour$q$,$q$The old steel bridge at the north end of the Bund, with Lujiazui lighting up behind it.$q$,$q$20-70 / 35mm$q$,'blue','17:05','must','planned',5,'spot',null,31.245307,121.485744,$q$At the north end of the Bund promenade, where Suzhou Creek meets the river. Walk the promenade end and the creek bank until the bridge's steel truss lines up with the Pudong towers. Sunset 4:52, blue hour until about 5:20.$q$,$q$- The bridge's steel truss with the Pearl Tower behind, both lighting up — 20-70.
- Cars and cyclists crossing the bridge, slightly blurred — 35mm, braced, about 1/4s.
- The Broadway Mansions behind the bridge as its windows light up — 20-70.$q$,$q$No tripod: brace on the stone wall. 35mm at f/2, about 1/4s, ISO 800, 2-second timer. On the 20-70 at f/4: 1/15s, ISO 3200. If you bring the mini tripod, this is a spot for it: ISO 100, f/8, 5–15s for smooth water.$q$,false),
(18,163,839,$q$Anfu and Julu Roads$q$,$q$Plane-tree streets of cafés and shops, the leaves turning gold in late November.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'midday','11:30','want','planned',6,'area',500,31.215618,121.438035,$q$Anfu Road, then north to Julu Road. Walk slowly; stand at crossings for the long views down the streets.$q$,$q$- Yellow plane leaves over the street, a cyclist below — 70-200 from a crossing, compressing the trees.
- Café windows and the people in them — 70-200 from across the street.
- The old lane houses (lilong) behind the shops: washing poles, scooters — 20-70.
- Dappled shade on the walls — expose for the bright patches.$q$,null,false),
(18,163,841,$q$Jing'an Temple among the towers$q$,$q$Gold temple roofs against the glass skyscrapers of Nanjing West Road.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'afternoon','15:00','want','planned',7,'spot',null,31.225215,121.440792,$q$From across Nanjing West Road for the roofs against the towers, then inside the courtyard.$q$,$q$- Gold roof ridges stacked against office towers — 70-200 at 150–200.
- Incense smoke in the courtyard, backlit by the afternoon sun — 70-200.
- People lighting incense — 70-200, from a respectful distance.$q$,null,false),
(18,163,984,$q$1000 Trees across Suzhou Creek$q$,$q$Heatherwick's terraced building, a tree on every column, reflected in the creek at last light.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'golden','16:30','want','planned',8,'spot',null,31.250871,121.440889,$q$From the riverside path across the creek from the building. Sunset about 4:52.$q$,$q$- The whole terraced front reflected in the creek, last sun on it — 20-70.
- The columns and trees as a repeating pattern — 70-200 at 100–200.
- A boat or a rower crossing in front — 70-200.$q$,null,false),
(18,164,844,$q$Humble Administrator's Garden at opening$q$,$q$Pavilions, moon gates and still water before the tour groups arrive.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'morning','07:35','must','planned',9,'area',300,31.326353,120.624712,$q$In at the 7:30 opening; head straight for the central pond while it's empty.$q$,$q$- A view framed through a moon gate or a lattice window — 20-70.
- Pavilions reflected in the pond before any wind — 20-70.
- Late-autumn colour against white walls and grey tiles — 70-200.
- A gardener sweeping leaves — 70-200.$q$,$q$The white walls blow out quickly in low sun: expose for them and lift the shadows later.$q$,false),
(18,164,845,$q$Suzhou Museum$q$,$q$I. M. Pei's white walls and grey stone, and a rock garden cut like paper against a wall.$q$,$q$20-70$q$,'any','09:00','want','planned',10,'spot',null,31.32525,120.623569,$q$Next door to the garden; in at the 9:00 opening.$q$,$q$- The rock garden: flat stone slabs set against the white wall, reflected in the pond — 20-70 at 35–50, straight on.
- Geometric skylights and timber louvres throwing stripes of light — 20-70.
- Visitors framed in the hexagonal windows — 20-70.$q$,$q$Photos are usually allowed; no flash. Follow any signs in the special exhibitions.$q$,false),
(18,164,846,$q$Pingjiang Road canal$q$,$q$Suzhou's old canal street: stone bridges, whitewashed houses and boats.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'midday','12:00','want','planned',11,'area',600,31.314929,120.629691,$q$Walk the canal end to end; the Couple's Garden is just off it.$q$,$q$- A boatwoman rowing under a stone bridge — 70-200 from the next bridge along.
- Whitewashed walls and black tiles reflected in the canal — 20-70.
- The side lanes off the main street: washing, bikes, cats — 20-70.
- Steaming baskets at the dumpling shops — 20-70.$q$,null,false),
(18,165,852,$q$The Star Ferry$q$,$q$The 1950s green-and-white ferries across Victoria Harbour.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'morning','10:30','want','planned',12,'spot',null,22.293541,114.167987,$q$Tsim Sha Tsui pier. Ride the lower deck for the water, the upper deck for the view.$q$,$q$- The island skyline from the deck, the ferry's rail in the foreground — 20-70.
- A deckhand throwing the mooring rope as you dock — 20-70.
- Commuters on the flip-back wooden benches — 20-70 at 35, from the end of the row.
- The other ferry passing mid-harbour — 70-200.$q$,null,false),
(18,165,852,$q$Sheung Wan's dried-seafood streets$q$,$q$Shops of dried scallops, fish maw and mushrooms, and the workers moving it all.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'midday','12:00','want','planned',13,'area',400,22.287317,114.133674,$q$Des Voeux Road West and the streets around it, west of Sheung Wan station.$q$,$q$- Shopfronts stacked with dried goods in sacks and jars — 20-70.
- Workers hauling sacks on trolleys — 70-200 from across the street.
- Goods drying in trays on the pavement — 20-70.
- Old hand-lettered shop signs — 70-200.$q$,null,false),
(18,166,855,$q$The Peak from Lugard Road$q$,$q$The classic view over Central's towers to Kowloon, from the quiet loop path.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'morning','08:30','must','planned',14,'area',500,22.276481,114.141919,$q$Lugard Road, the loop path from the Peak Tower. The best of the view is about 10 minutes along, at the railing.$q$,$q$- The whole harbour panorama — 20-70 at 20–30, or several frames to stitch.
- Central's towers stacked on each other — 70-200 at 150–200, the morning light from the side.
- A walker on the path with the city below — 20-70.
- Winter is often hazy; haze suits the long lens.$q$,null,false),
(18,166,856,$q$Mong Kok's goldfish and flower markets$q$,$q$Walls of bagged goldfish, flower stalls, and the old bird garden.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'afternoon','13:30','want','planned',15,'area',600,22.322884,114.16983,$q$Tung Choi Street (Goldfish Street), then north to the Flower Market and the Bird Garden.$q$,$q$- Walls of bagged goldfish hanging in the shopfronts, lit from behind — 20-70 close, or 70-200 for one bag.
- Flower sellers wrapping bunches — 70-200.
- Bird Garden: old men with their birdcages — 70-200 from a distance.$q$,null,false),
(18,166,857,$q$Sham Shui Po into the evening$q$,$q$Street food, fabric stalls and neon as a working neighbourhood lights up.$q$,$q$35mm / 85mm$q$,'blue','17:45','want','planned',16,'area',500,22.329927,114.162331,$q$Apliu Street and the blocks around it. Sunset 5:39; blue hour until about 6.$q$,$q$- Apliu Street's stalls of old electronics and cables under bare bulbs — 35mm.
- A cook in the steam at a food stall — 85mm wide open.
- Rolls of cloth on the fabric street, a shopkeeper measuring — 85mm.
- Signs overhead as the sky goes blue — 35mm.$q$,null,false),
(18,167,null,$q$Monster Building, Quarry Bay$q$,$q$Five joined residential blocks wrapped around a small courtyard, looking straight up.$q$,$q$20-70$q$,'any','08:15','maybe','planned',17,'spot',null,22.284029,114.212328,$q$On the way to Dragon's Back: Quarry Bay MTR, then 5 minutes' walk. The courtyard is behind the shops on King's Road.$q$,$q$- Straight up from the courtyard, the walls of windows closing in — 20-70 at 20.
- One lit window or hanging laundry in the pattern — 20-70 at 70.$q$,$q$These are people's homes: be quiet, keep out of the way, and follow any no-photo signs.$q$,false),
(18,167,858,$q$Dragon's Back ridge$q$,$q$The ridge walk above the sea, ending at Big Wave Bay.$q$,$q$20-70$q$,'morning','09:45','want','planned',18,'area',1200,22.239258,114.241993,$q$The ridge itself, about 30 minutes up from the To Tei Wan trailhead.$q$,$q$- The ridge path running ahead with hikers on it, sea on both sides — 20-70 at 20–35.
- Shek O and Big Wave Bay below — 20-70.
- Paragliders launching off the ridge, if they're flying — 20-70 at 70.$q$,null,false),
(18,167,864,$q$Harbour at dusk from West Kowloon$q$,$q$Hong Kong Island's skyline lighting up across the water.$q$,$q$20-70 / 35mm$q$,'blue','17:55','must','planned',19,'area',500,22.299729,114.157733,$q$The waterfront by M+ and the Art Park, looking across the harbour to Central and Wan Chai. Sunset 5:39, blue hour until about 6:05.$q$,$q$- The island skyline as the lights come on with the sky still blue — 20-70 at 24–35, braced on the sea wall.
- M+'s huge lit facade behind people on the lawn — 20-70 or 35.
- A ferry or a red-sailed junk crossing — 35mm at about 1/4s.
- Silhouettes along the sea wall — 35mm.$q$,$q$No tripod: brace on the sea wall. 35mm at f/2, about 1/4s, ISO 800, 2-second timer. On the 20-70 at f/4: 1/15s, ISO 3200. If you bring the mini tripod, this is a spot for it: ISO 100, f/8, 5–15s for smooth water.$q$,false),
(18,168,962,$q$Yuet Tung China Works$q$,$q$Hand-painted porcelain, the same family since 1928.$q$,$q$85mm / 35mm$q$,'any','14:30','want','planned',20,'spot',null,22.322987,114.210743,$q$The workshop in Kowloon Bay. Ask before photographing the painters, and buy something.$q$,$q$- A painter's hand and brush on a plate — 85mm wide open, close.
- Shelves stacked with finished pieces — 35mm.
- The painter at the bench in window light — 35mm.$q$,null,false),
(18,170,869,$q$Yangtze River cable car$q$,$q$The red cable car across the river, towers on the cliffs on both sides.$q$,$q$20-70$q$,'morning','09:00','want','planned',21,'spot',null,29.55804,106.584438,$q$Ride from the south station; the north station is on Xinhua Road in Yuzhong.$q$,$q$- The river, ships and the city on the cliffs through the window — 20-70, lens hood against the glass.
- The other car passing mid-river — 20-70 at 70.
- Fog is normal in December: the towers fade in layers. Expose for the fog.$q$,null,false),
(18,170,989,$q$The cable car past Baixiangju$q$,$q$The red cable car gliding past an old riverside apartment block.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'morning','10:00','must','planned',22,'spot',null,29.558528,106.581348,$q$Baixiangju, a 5–10 minute walk down from the north station.$q$,$q$- A red car gliding past the building — 70-200 to stack the car against it. One comes every few minutes.
- The building's stairways and laundry — 20-70.
- People live here: keep quiet and don't block the stairs.$q$,null,false),
(18,170,870,$q$Shancheng Trail and the old stairways$q$,$q$Cliffside walkways and stairs above the Yangtze.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'midday','11:30','want','planned',23,'area',600,29.555303,106.562056,$q$The trail starts at Shancheng Lane in Qixinggang and runs along the cliffs.$q$,$q$- Stairs dropping down the hill into fog, one person climbing — 70-200 from the top.
- Mahjong tables and tea on the landings — 70-200.
- The river and bridges from the cliff walkway — 20-70.$q$,null,false),
(18,170,871,$q$Liziba: the train through the building$q$,$q$The monorail running straight through a residential block.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'afternoon','15:00','want','planned',24,'spot',null,29.556673,106.53441,$q$The viewing platform below Liziba station (李子坝站观景平台).$q$,$q$- A train entering the building — 70-200 from the platform. They come every few minutes.
- Wider, with the block's full height — 20-70.$q$,null,false),
(18,170,872,$q$Hongyadong from Qiansimen Bridge$q$,$q$The stacked stilt-house complex lit gold above the river.$q$,$q$35mm / 85mm$q$,'blue','18:15','must','planned',25,'spot',null,29.567808,106.575349,$q$On the walkway of Qiansimen Bridge, looking back at Hongyadong. Sunset 5:55, blue hour until about 6:20; the lights come on around dusk.$q$,$q$- Hongyadong's lit facade stacked above the river — 35mm.
- The crowd on the bridge photographing it — 85mm.
- The river traffic below, lit boats — 35mm.$q$,$q$The bridge shakes with traffic, so bracing doesn't help much: shoot faster. 35mm at f/1.4–2, 1/60s, ISO 3200–6400.$q$,false),
(18,171,875,$q$Three Natural Bridges$q$,$q$Stone arches over a deep gorge.$q$,$q$20-70$q$,'any','10:30','must','planned',26,'area',1200,29.439934,107.786329,$q$On the gorge floor, after the elevator down.$q$,$q$- An arch from the gorge floor with people tiny underneath — 20-70 at 20, vertical.
- Water and mist in the shafts of light — 20-70.
- Take three frames at different exposures: the sky through the arch and the shade are far apart.$q$,null,false),
(18,171,918,$q$Tianfu Official Post from above$q$,$q$The restored post house's dark roofs between the gorge walls.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'any','11:00','want','planned',27,'spot',null,29.437948,107.792515,$q$From the walkway on the way down, before you reach the post house.$q$,$q$- The tiled roofs filling the frame — 70-200.
- The post house small in the gorge — 20-70.$q$,null,false),
(18,172,902,$q$Yulong River at dusk$q$,$q$Karst peaks going blue over the river, from the hotel's own bank.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'golden','17:15','want','planned',28,'area',800,24.740363,110.475376,$q$From the riverbank by the hotel (in Zhudouzhai village, by Qinglong Bridge). Sunset 5:49.$q$,$q$- Layers of peaks going blue in the haze — 70-200 to stack them.
- Bamboo rafts tied up at the landing — 20-70.
- Farmers walking home along the field banks — 70-200.$q$,null,false),
(18,173,910,$q$Bamboo raft on the Yulong$q$,$q$The river through the fields and peaks, from the raft.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'morning','09:00','must','planned',29,'area',2000,24.740363,110.475376,$q$From the hotel's landing, downstream about 1.5 hours.$q$,$q$- The raftsman poling at the back, peaks ahead — turn around, 20-70 at 24.
- Rafts ahead dropping over the small weirs — 70-200.
- Morning mist on the peaks and their reflections — 20-70.
- Water buffalo and farmers on the bank — 70-200.$q$,$q$Keep the strap on; the rafts lurch at the weirs. Have a plastic bag ready for the camera.$q$,false),
(18,173,904,$q$The 20-yuan view$q$,$q$The Li River bend printed on the back of the 20-yuan note.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'midday','13:30','must','planned',30,'spot',null,24.925104,110.51664,$q$Out from Xingping pier on the raft; the view is on the way.$q$,$q$- The river bend with the peaks reflected — 20-70. Hold a 20-yuan note up in the frame for the joke.
- Ridges of peaks stacked in haze — 70-200.
- Other bamboo rafts on the green water — 70-200.$q$,null,false),
(18,173,905,$q$Xingping old town at dusk$q$,$q$Old lanes of wooden shopfronts, then the riverbank as the sun goes.$q$,$q$20-70 / 35mm$q$,'golden','17:15','want','planned',31,'area',500,24.9176,110.534033,$q$The old town's lanes, then the riverbank at its edge. Sunset 5:49.$q$,$q$- Wooden shopfronts and people in doorways — 20-70.
- The river and peaks from the bank as the light goes — 20-70.
- Cormorant fishermen pose by the river for a small fee; worth paying for — 20-70.
- Dinner lanterns coming on in the lanes — 35mm.$q$,null,false),
(18,174,909,$q$Li River rooftop at dusk$q$,$q$The river and peaks from the resort's roof as the sky goes pink, then blue.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'golden','17:20','want','planned',32,'spot',null,24.917922,110.504654,$q$The resort's rooftop (the resort is at Liandao Bay, 镰刀湾). Sunset 5:49, blue hour until about 6:15.$q$,$q$- The river bend and peaks as the sky changes — 20-70.
- Layers of peaks fading into haze — 70-200.
- A fishing raft with a lamp on the dark water — 70-200.$q$,$q$No tripod: rest the camera on the roof ledge. 20-70 at f/8, about 1/2s, ISO 200, 2-second timer, a few frames. If you bring the mini tripod, this is a spot for it: ISO 100, f/8, 5–15s for smooth water.$q$,false),
(18,175,null,$q$Laozhai Hill at sunrise$q$,$q$The Li River bend and its peaks from the hill above Xingping, at first light.$q$,$q$20-70 / 70-200$q$,'golden','07:15','want','planned',33,'spot',null,24.917735,110.520504,$q$Laozhai Hill, right above Xingping town: a steep stair climb from the river. Start in the dark with a headlamp; arrange a car from the resort the night before. Sunrise 7:12.$q$,$q$- The river bend below with mist in the valleys — 20-70.
- Layer after layer of peaks in the first light — 70-200.
- The small pavilion at the top with the view behind — 20-70.$q$,$q$Not in the koji itinerary: add it before the river trail if you want it.$q$,false),
(18,175,982,$q$Li River walking trail$q$,$q$Rafts, fishermen and villages along the water between the peaks.$q$,$q$70-200 / 20-70$q$,'morning','10:30','want','planned',34,'area',3000,24.917922,110.504654,$q$Along the river from the resort.$q$,$q$- Bamboo rafts and fishermen with the peaks behind — 70-200.
